# SmartFridge Vision MVP — configuration
#
# Copy this file to ".env" and fill in your API key. The .env file is git-ignored
# and must never be committed.
#
# These three variables point the app at any OpenAI-compatible VISION
# chat-completions endpoint, so the provider is swappable without code changes.
# The defaults below target OpenRouter's free vision tier (models with a ":free"
# suffix cost nothing). See the README for how to repoint them at Groq, Google
# Gemini, or any other OpenAI-compatible vision provider.
#
# NOTE: free model ids rotate often. Verify the current free vision model id at
# https://openrouter.ai/models (filter: input = image, price = free) before relying
# on the default below. Get a key at https://openrouter.ai/keys.

VISION_API_KEY=
VISION_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
VISION_MODEL=inclusionai/ling-3.0-flash-vl:free

# --- Fallbacks (optional) ----------------------------------------------------
# Free tiers rate-limit hard and rotate model ids, so you can define up to THREE
# fallbacks. If the primary above fails (rate limit, auth error, unreachable, or an
# unreadable response), the app automatically tries fallback 1, then 2, then 3, and
# only shows an error if every attempt fails.
#
# Each fallback can override any of the three variables. Anything you leave blank is
# inherited from the slot before it — so to just try different models on the same
# key/provider, set only the VISION_MODEL_* lines. A fallback is ignored unless at
# least one of its variables is filled in. (Verify current free ids at
# https://openrouter.ai/models — input=image, price=free.)

# Fallback 1 — e.g. a different free model on the same OpenRouter key:
VISION_MODEL_2=nex-agi/nex-n2.5-pro:free
# VISION_API_KEY_2=
# VISION_BASE_URL_2=

# Fallback 2 — e.g. yet another free model:
VISION_MODEL_3=nex-agi/nex-n2.5-mini:free
# VISION_API_KEY_3=
# VISION_BASE_URL_3=

# Fallback 3 — e.g. a second key, or a different provider entirely (set all three):
# VISION_API_KEY_4=
# VISION_BASE_URL_4=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
# VISION_MODEL_4=meta-llama/llama-4-scout-17b-16e-instruct

# --- Storage -----------------------------------------------------------------
# History is stored via libSQL (a SQLite fork). Locally it writes to a plain file;
# in the cloud it can talk to a hosted Turso database instead (see the README's
# "Deploy for free" section). The target is chosen automatically at runtime.
#
# Local file (default): path to the SQLite file that records inventory history
# (every scan is saved with its timestamp). Created automatically on first run; lives
# in the project folder and is git-ignored. Uncomment to change the location.
# DATABASE_PATH=smartfridge.db
#
# Turso (cloud): if TURSO_DATABASE_URL is set, the app connects to that database
# instead of the local file. Get both values from your Turso dashboard. Leave these
# UNSET for local development. The auth token is a secret — never commit it.
# TURSO_DATABASE_URL=libsql://your-db-name.turso.io
# TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN=
